    skos:closeMatch <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4087> ;
    skos:definition "a volatile alkali, a compound of azote and hydrogen; several combinations of it enter into commerce, as liquid or caustic ammonin, spirits of hartshorn, and sulphate of ammonia from the liquor of gas-works. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 22]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_ammonia" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ammonia"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0506 (Chemical Manufactures and Products Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 22."@en ;
    <ontology/attestationBasis/#resource> "document_attested" ;
